  "text": "ibed in paragraph (2) shall be one dollar for each dollar excluded by subsection (a). (B) Credit carryover reduction The reductions described in subparagraphs (B), (C), and (G) shall be 33⅓ cents for each dollar excluded by subsection (a). The reduction described in subparagraph (F) in any passive activity credit carryover shall be 33⅓ cents for each dollar excluded by subsection (a). (4) Ordering rules (A) Reductions made after determination of tax for year The reductions described in paragraph (2) shall be made after the determination of the tax imposed by this chapter for the taxable year of the discharge. (B) Reductions under subparagraph (A) or (D) of paragraph (2) The reductions described in subparagraph (A) or (D) of paragraph (2) (as the case may be) shall be made first in the loss for the taxable year of the discharge and then in the carryovers to such taxable year in the order of the taxable years from which each such carryover arose. (C) Reductions under subparagraphs (B) and (G) of paragraph (2) The reductions described in subparagraphs (B) and (G) of paragraph (2) shall be made in the order in which carryovers are taken into account under this chapter for the taxable year of the discharge. (5) Election to apply reduction first against depreciable property (A) In general The taxpayer may elect to apply any portion of the reduction referred to in paragraph (1) to the reduction under section 1017 of the basis of the depreciable property of the taxpayer. (B) Limitation The amount to which an election under subparagraph (A) applies shall not exceed the aggregate adjusted bases of the depreciable property held by the taxpayer as of the beginning of the taxable year following the taxable year in which the discharge occurs. (C) Other tax attributes not reduced Paragraph (2) shall not apply to any amount to which an election under this paragraph applies.",
