  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(a) General rule (1) Wholly worthless debts There shall be allowed as a deduction any debt which becomes worthless within the taxable year. (2) Partially worthless debts When satisfied that a debt is recoverable only in part, the Secretary may allow such debt, in an amount not in excess of the part charged off within the taxable year, as a deduction.",
