  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(a) General rule Except as provided in subsections (b) and (c), if— (1) the taxpayer receives property which would be permitted to be received under section 351 or 361 without the recognition of gain if it were the sole consideration, and (2) as part of the consideration, another party to the exchange assumes a liability of the taxpayer, then such assumption shall not be treated as money or other property, and shall not prevent the exchange from being within the provisions of section 351 or 361, as the case may be.",
