  "text": "(a) Excess credits (1) In general Under regulations, if an ownership change occurs with respect to a corporation, the amount of any excess credit for any taxable year which may be used in any post-change year shall be limited to an amount determined on the basis of the tax liability which is attributable to so much of the taxable income as does not exceed the section 382 limitation for such post-change year to the extent available after the application of section 382 and subsections (b) and (c) of this section. (2) Excess credit For purposes of paragraph (1), the term “excess credit” means— (A) any unused general business credit of the corporation under section 39, and (B) any unused minimum tax credit of the corporation under section 53.",
