  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(g) No books kept; no accounting period Except as provided in section 443 (relating to returns for periods of less than 12 months), the taxpayer’s taxable year shall be the calendar year if— (1) the taxpayer keeps no books; (2) the taxpayer does not have an annual accounting period; or (3) the taxpayer has an annual accounting period, but such period does not qualify as a fiscal year.",
