  "sourceUrl": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/483",
  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(b) Total unstated interest For purposes of this section, the term “total unstated interest” means, with respect to a contract for the sale or exchange of property, an amount equal to the excess of— (1) the sum of the payments to which this section applies which are due under the contract, over (2) the sum of the present values of such payments and the present values of any interest payments due under the contract. For purposes of the preceding sentence, the present value of a payment shall be determined under the rules of section 1274(b)(2) using a discount rate equal to the applicable Federal rate determined under section 1274(d).",
