  "sourceUrl": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/503",
  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(a) Denial of exemption to organizations engaged in prohibited transactions (1) General rule An organization described in paragraph (17) or (18) of section 501(c), or described in section 401(a) and referred to in section 4975(g) (2) or (3), shall not be exempt from taxation under section 501(a) if it has engaged in a prohibited transaction. (2) Taxable years affected An organization described in paragraph (1) shall be denied exemption from taxation under section 501(a) by reason of paragraph (1) only for taxable years after the taxable year during which it is notified by the Secretary that it has engaged in a prohibited transaction, unless such organization entered into such prohibited transaction with the purpose of diverting corpus or income of the organization from its exempt purposes, and such transaction involved a substantial part of the corpus or income of such organization.",
