  "text": "(d) Presumption that foreign trust has United States beneficiary If a United States person directly or indirectly transfers property to a foreign trust (other than a trust described in section 6048(a)(3)(B)(ii)), the Secretary may treat such trust as having a United States beneficiary for purposes of applying this section to such transfer unless such person— (1) submits such information to the Secretary as the Secretary may require with respect to such transfer, and (2) demonstrates to the satisfaction of the Secretary that such trust satisfies the requirements of subparagraphs (A) and (B) of subsection (c)(1).",
