  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(e) Interest on United States obligations received by banks organized in possessions In the case of a corporation created or organized in, or under the law of, a possession of the United States which is carrying on the banking business in a possession of the United States, interest on obligations of the United States which is not portfolio interest (as defined in section 881(c)(2)) shall— (1) for purposes of this subpart, be treated as income which is effectively connected with the conduct of a trade or business within the United States, and (2) shall be taxable as provided in subsection (a)(1) whether or not such corporation is engaged in trade or business within the United States during the taxable year.",
