  "sourceUrl": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/894",
  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(b) Permanent establishment in United States For purposes of applying any exemption from, or reduction of, any tax provided by any treaty to which the United States is a party with respect to income which is not effectively connected with the conduct of a trade or business within the United States, a nonresident alien individual or a foreign corporation shall be deemed not to have a permanent establishment in the United States at any time during the taxable year. This subsection shall not apply in respect of the tax computed under section 877(b).",
