  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(b) Certain residents of possessions considered citizens of the United States A donor who is a citizen of the United States and a resident of a possession thereof shall, for purposes of the tax imposed by this chapter, be considered a “citizen” of the United States within the meaning of that term wherever used in this title unless he acquired his United States citizenship solely by reason of (1) his being a citizen of such possession of the United States, or (2) his birth or residence within such possession of the United States.",
