  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(g) Application of section in case of tax withheld on wages (1) In general For purposes of applying this section, the amount of the credit allowed under section 31 for the taxable year shall be deemed a payment of estimated tax, and an equal part of such amount shall be deemed paid on each due date for such taxable year, unless the taxpayer establishes the dates on which all amounts were actually withheld, in which case the amounts so withheld shall be deemed payments of estimated tax on the dates on which such amounts were actually withheld. (2) Separate application The taxpayer may apply paragraph (1) separately with respect to— (A) wage withholding, and (B) all other amounts withheld for which credit is allowed under section 31.",
