  "ingestedAt": "2026-06-27T00:00:00Z",
  "text": "(c) Activities of subordinates (1) In general For purposes of subsection (a), the term “procures” includes— (A) ordering (or otherwise causing) a subordinate to do an act, and (B) knowing of, and not attempting to prevent, participation by a subordinate in an act. (2) Subordinate For purposes of paragraph (1), the term “subordinate” means any other person (whether or not a director, officer, employee, or agent of the taxpayer involved) over whose activities the person has direction, supervision, or control.",
